  ('378626999484262858', 'The House on Carroll Street', 1988, 'Drama, Thriller', 'Peter Yates, Michael Ballhaus', 'Walter Bernstein', 'Kelly McGillis, Jeff Daniels, Mandy Patinkin, Jessica Tandy, Jonathan Hogan, Remak Ramsay, Kenneth Welsh, Christopher Buchholz', 'PG', 'A reporter, fired after refusing to give names to a 1951 House Un-American Activities Committee, takes a part-time job as companion to an old lady. While working she overhears a noisy argument in the neighboring house, being conducted largely in German and involving her HUAC prosecutor. She begins to investigate, enlisting the help of the FBI Agent initially detailed to surveil her.', 'A reporter, fired after refusing to give names to a 1951 House Un-American Activities Committee, takes a part-time job as companion to an old lady. While working she overhears a noisy argument in the neighboring house, being conducted largely in German and involving her HUAC prosecutor. She begins to investigate, enlisting the help of the FBI Agent initially detailed to surveil her.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/kqYP8ZWYTObqzrGEDafUSfEQyFg.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:75889'),
  ('182653725170464784', 'The House on Chelouche Street', 1973, 'Drama', 'Moshé Mizrahi', 'Yerech Guber, Rachel Fabien', 'Ofer Shalhin, Gila Almagor, Yosef Shiloach, Michal Bat-Adam, Etti Grotes, Avner Hizkiyahu, Shaike Ophir, Rolf Brin', null, 'A fatherless family immigrates to Israel from Egypt during the British Mandate period. The film traces the hardships the family suffers in the politically unstable country.', 'A fatherless family immigrates to Israel from Egypt during the British Mandate period. The film traces the hardships the family suffers in the politically unstable country.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/jhqmrjeWSkEtwXRYXDsB3KW4jVG.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:117486'),
