  ('275053667759817081', 'The Husbands, the Wives, the Lovers', 1989, 'Drama, Comedy', 'Pascal Thomas, Renan Pollès', 'Pascal Thomas, François Caviglioli', 'Jean-François Stévenin, Susan Moncur, Clément Thomas, Emilie Thomas, Daniel Ceccaldi, Michel Robin, Vanessa Guedj, Anne Guinou', null, 'In the summer holidays, a group of women stay behind in Paris whilst their husbands and children take a vacation on the sunny Island of Ré. The women – wives, frustrated spinsters and adolescents – profit from their new-found freedom to sort out their love lives and the men indulge their earthy passions with no less enthusiasm. Only the children seems capable of rising above this infantile summer madness...', 'In the summer holidays, a group of women stay behind in Paris whilst their husbands and children take a vacation on the sunny Island of Ré. The women – wives, frustrated spinsters and adolescents – profit from their new-found freedom to sort out their love lives and the men indulge their earthy passions with no less enthusiasm. Only the children seems capable of rising above this infantile summer madness...', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/eVMqtah7eqq9aZxAc4ZWXEtDhQY.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:173999'),
  ('973849138672591137', 'The Hussar of Death', 1925, 'History', 'Pedro Sienna', 'Hugo Silva, Pedro Sienna', 'Pedro Sienna, Clara Werther, Piet Van Ravenstein, Dolores Anziani, María de Hannig, Hugo Silva', null, 'Depicts the deeds of Chilean national hero Manuel Rodriguez and the events of the Chilean War of Independence against Spain in the early 1800s.', 'Depicts the deeds of Chilean national hero Manuel Rodriguez and the events of the Chilean War of Independence against Spain in the early 1800s.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/nfn3dbQc3wQIhuHzEfPJJIOQ9Ow.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:184407'),
  ('600340587745792077', 'The Hussars', 1955, 'War, Comedy, Adventure', 'Alex Joffé, Jean Bourgoin', null, 'Bernard Blier, Giovanna Ralli, Bourvil, Georges Wilson, Clelia Matania, Virna Lisi, Alberto Bonucci, Carlo Campanini', null, 'Brigadier Le Gouce and Private Flicot lose their horses during a campaign in Italy. To avoid looking ridiculous, the two hussars cross the country in search of their mounts. But when they are mistaken for deserters, their regiment gives chase.', 'Brigadier Le Gouce and Private Flicot lose their horses during a campaign in Italy. To avoid looking ridiculous, the two hussars cross the country in search of their mounts. But when they are mistaken for deserters, their regiment gives chase.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/a4c632Vz99gmYSRoqVamOW2bui1.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:106579'),
  ('308342682498585813', 'The Hussy', 1979, 'Drama', 'Jacques Doillon, Philippe Rousselot, Guy Chalaud', 'Denis Ferraris, Jacques Doillon', 'Claude Hébert, Madeleine Desdevises, Paulette Lahaye, Juliette Le Cauchoix, Fernand Decaean, Dominique Besnehard, Odette Maestrini, Ginette Mazure', null, 'Twenty-year old misfit François earns his living by gathering boxes and bottles to resell to local shopkeepers. He lives with his grossly insensitive mother and stepfather. Mado is a gawky 11-year old, who is neglected by her family because of the oddness of the way she expresses her affection. For reasons which never become clear, François kidnaps Mado, and takes her to live with him in the attic of his parents'' home. Instead of feeling fear, Mado enters into the spirit of the abduction, and they joust with one another, increasingly finding love and comfort in their relationship. When the police come upon them, however, they put an entirely different interpretation on their behavior.', 'Twenty-year old misfit François earns his living by gathering boxes and bottles to resell to local shopkeepers. He lives with his grossly insensitive mother and stepfather. Mado is a gawky 11-year old, who is neglected by her family because of the oddness of the way she expresses her affection. For reasons which never become clear, François kidnaps Mado, and takes her to live with him in the attic of his parents'' home. Instead of feeling fear, Mado enters into the spirit of the abduction, and they joust with one another, increasingly finding love and comfort in their relationship. When the police come upon them, however, they put an entirely different interpretation on their behavior.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/cOB9mmC9qgzU9gisj48fgCSn2Nn.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:63113'),
  ('551986637546142768', 'The Hustle', 2019, 'Comedy, Crime', 'Chris Addison, Michael Coulter, Mark Goddard', 'Stanley Shapiro, Paul Henning', 'Rebel Wilson, Anne Hathaway, Alex Sharp, Dean Norris, Timothy Simons, Ingrid Oliver, Nicholas Woodeson, Hannah Waddingham', 'PG-13', 'Two female scam artists, one low rent and the other high class, compete to swindle a naïve tech prodigy out of his fortune. A remake of the 1988 comedy "Dirty Rotten Scoundrels."', 'Two female scam artists, one low rent and the other high class, compete to swindle a naïve tech prodigy out of his fortune. A remake of the 1988 comedy "Dirty Rotten Scoundrels."', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/qZniBGQRESLIfxw6GeZLZ2G1osa.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:449562'),
